    {
      "id": "claim_aaac0d52d0734a69b0b0600000f286dd",
      "statement": "Durability modes balance power-loss resilience and write throughput: Lazy (default) updates mmap/page cache without per-mutation msync, survives process crashes, requires explicit flush for power-loss safety; RangeAsync asynchronously flushes modified byte ranges; Strict synchronously flushes modified byte ranges; LegacyWholeMmapAsync asynchronously flushes entire virtual memory map after each mutation.",
